{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Rule 6c-11 requires an ETF to maintain a free, publicly accessible website that discloses:\n\n- **Holdings:** each business day before market open, the prior-day portfolio holdings used to calculate the next NAV—not just the creation/redemption basket.\n- **Daily pricing:** closing market price, NAV, and premium or discount. If the premium/discount exceeds 2% for more than seven consecutive trading days, explain the circumstances, likely cause, and any steps being taken; keep the explanation posted until it no longer exceeds 2%.\n- **Premium/discount history:** a table or chart covering the most recently completed calendar year and completed quarters of the current year.\n- **Bid-ask spread:** the median spread over the prior 30 calendar days, updated daily.\n\nCreation/redemption baskets are disclosed separately to authorized participants before the next NAV calculation; they need not be posted publicly under Rule 6c-11."}}
